From c195fa47b005e78adc5be6b8f40bd1edc2a094f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wise <47094117+tjwise99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:53:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] oeqa: parselogs_rpi imports cleanly against scarthgap's
 parselogs

parselogs_rpi.py referenced two module-level names, ignore_errors and
common_errors, that this file's own `from oeqa.runtime.cases.parselogs
import *` never provided even when it was written: poky scarthgap's
parselogs.py keeps ignore_errors as a class attribute on ParseLogsTest
(populated from parselogs-ignores-*.txt resource files via
load_machine_ignores()), not a module global, and defines no
common_errors at all. Every oeqa test run that reaches test discovery
imports every case file under every layer's lib/oeqa/runtime/cases/ to
build its registry, so this file's NameError at import time fails
do_testimage outright, before any case -- rpi's own or any other
layer's -- gets a chance to run.

rpi_errors was an empty list; removing it and the four
ignore_errors[...] assignments it fed loses no actual ignore content,
only the names that do not resolve. The import and the
ParseLogsTestRpi subclass are unchanged.

This cannot be a bbappend: lib/oeqa is a Python module tree consumed by
bitbake's oeqa loader, not a recipe, so there is no do_install or
equivalent task to append into.

Upstream submission: suitable -- a straightforward compatibility fix,
not specific to this fork. Not yet submitted; not upstreamed as of
meta-raspberrypi master b2669c24bb577e1a48d841a60cfc0719f9ee1ff4
(2026-09-24), which still carries the same two code paths unchanged.

Applied by kas at checkout (see includes/platforms/raspberrypi.yaml).
---
 lib/oeqa/runtime/cases/parselogs_rpi.py | 7 -------
 1 file changed, 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/oeqa/runtime/cases/parselogs_rpi.py b/lib/oeqa/runtime/cases/parselogs_rpi.py
index 49226ae..06c9bb9 100644
--- a/lib/oeqa/runtime/cases/parselogs_rpi.py
+++ b/lib/oeqa/runtime/cases/parselogs_rpi.py
@@ -1,12 +1,5 @@
 from oeqa.runtime.cases.parselogs import *
 
-rpi_errors = [
-]
-
-ignore_errors['raspberrypi4'] = rpi_errors + common_errors
-ignore_errors['raspberrypi4-64'] = rpi_errors + common_errors
-ignore_errors['raspberrypi3'] = rpi_errors + common_errors
-ignore_errors['raspberrypi3-64'] = rpi_errors + common_errors
 
 class ParseLogsTestRpi(ParseLogsTest):
     pass
